Body:
Adding quantitative data to this issue: the `<available_skills>` block introduced in v1.16.0 causes a 5-7x cost increase on DeepSeek due to defeated prompt caching.

**Measured impact (single DeepSeek v4-pro user):**

| Metric | Pre-upgrade (May, v1.15.x) | Post-upgrade (June 8, v1.16.x) |
|---|---|---|
| Cache miss rate (pro) | 1-2% | 10-15% |
| Daily cost | ~$0.36/day | ~$5.03/day (one day) |
| Cache miss tokens/day | 1-2M | 8-14M |

**Why it matters for cost:** DeepSeek charges cache misses at 120x the cache-hit rate ($0.000000435 vs $0.000000003625 per token). The skill listing block pushes the system prompt past the cache boundary.

**Effective workaround** (verified -- miss rate dropped from 14% to 1.59% after applying):

```json
{
  "agent": {
    "build": {
      "tools": {
        "skill": false
      }
    },
    "plan": {
      "tools": {
        "skill": false
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Restart opencode after applying. Verify via DeepSeek usage CSV at platform.deepseek.com.

```
import { tool, type Plugin } from "@opencode-ai/plugin"

export default (async () => ({
  tool: {
    add_numbers: tool({
      description: "Add two numbers and return their sum.",
      args: {
        a: tool.schema.number().describe("First number"),
        b: tool.schema.number().describe("Second number"),
      },
      async execute(args) {
        return `${args.a + args.b}`
      },
    }),
  },
})) satisfies Plugin

```

